.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_SEQUENCER 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_sequencer_new ,
.Nm dtfl_sequencer_push ,
.Nm dtfl_sequencer_next ,
.Nm dtfl_sequencer_free
.Nd shared totally ordered log across workers
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely_ops.h
.Ft dtfl_sequencer *
.Fn dtfl_sequencer_new "dtfl_worker *w" "const dtfl_type *type"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_sequencer_push "dtfl_sequencer *s" "const void *rec" "size_t len"
.Ft const void *
.Fn dtfl_sequencer_next "dtfl_sequencer *s" "size_t *len"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_sequencer_free "dtfl_sequencer *s"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A sequencer is a shared log that every worker observes in the same
order.
.Fn dtfl_sequencer_new
builds a dataflow that timestamps proposed records with the elapsed
time, broadcasts each to every worker, and delivers them in a total
order broken by the proposing worker and a per-worker counter.
Every worker must create its sequencers in the same order, over the
same record
.Fa type .
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_sequencer_push
proposes a record of
.Fa len
bytes.
It is not visible until the next worker step sends it and the elapsed
time frontier passes.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_sequencer_next
returns the next sequenced record and stores its length in
.Fa len ,
or
.Dv NULL
when none is ready.
The returned pointer is owned by the sequencer and stays valid until the
next call to
.Fn dtfl_sequencer_next
or
.Fn dtfl_sequencer_free .
Every worker sees the same records in the same order.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_sequencer_free
drops the sequencer; its dataflow releases its capability so the log
can wind down.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_sequencer_next
returns a record pointer, or
.Dv NULL
when the log has nothing ready.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dtfl_sequencer *s = dtfl_sequencer_new(worker, dtfl_type_u64());
unsigned char buf[8];
dtfl_put_u64(buf, value);
dtfl_sequencer_push(s, buf, sizeof buf);
dtfl_worker_step(worker);
const void *rec; size_t len;
while ((rec = dtfl_sequencer_next(s, &len)) != NULL)
	handle(rec, len);
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
These functions do not return error codes.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_barrier 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_execute 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
This is the C form of timely's
.Vt Sequencer
of
.Pa synchronization/sequence.rs .
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
A sequencer belongs to the worker thread that created it.
Records cross between workers through the dataflow's channels, not
through the handle, so the handle is used only on its own worker.
